    "title": "Concept 1: Speed",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Speed is a compound measure showing how fast something moves. It is calculated using the formula: <strong>Speed = Distance ÷ Time</strong>. Common units of speed are metres per second (m/s), kilometres per hour (km/h), and miles per hour (mph).</p>",
